      "message": "Consider expanding `test/subtract_test.cc` to cover the cases exercised by the new `subtract_avx2.c` paths:\n- `kValidBlockSize` (line 216) currently only tests square and 1:2 / 2:1 block sizes; adding the six 1:4 / 4:1 rectangular block sizes (`BLOCK_4X16`, `BLOCK_16X4`, `BLOCK_8X32`, `BLOCK_32X8`, `BLOCK_16X64`, `BLOCK_64X16`) would cover the new AVX2 `4xN`, `8xN`, and unrolled `16xN` paths on `4x16`, `8x32`, `16x4`, and `16x64`.\n- Also test `stride \u003e cols` and unaligned `src`/`pred` pointer offsets (plus 8-byte-aligned `diff` sub-block offsets for `cols \u003d\u003d 4`), since `CheckResult()` currently only tests `src_stride \u003d\u003d pred_stride \u003d\u003d diff_stride \u003d\u003d block_width_` on 32-byte-aligned base buffers.",
