      "side": 1,
      "message": "`subtract_block_4xn_avx2`, `subtract_block_8xn_avx2`, and `subtract_block_16xn_avx2` now all use `int32_t j \u003d rows \u003e\u003e 1; do { ... } while (--j !\u003d 0);` (removing `16xn`\u0027s previous 1-row remainder loop), and `32xn`/`64xn`/`128xn` also switch from `for` loops to `do { ... } while (--j !\u003d 0);`. While AV1 block/transform heights are always even and `\u003e\u003d 4`, adding `assert(rows \u003e\u003d 2 \u0026\u0026 (rows \u0026 1) \u003d\u003d 0)` in `4xn`/`8xn`/`16xn` and `assert(rows \u003e 0)` in `32xn`–`128xn` would guard against `j \u003d\u003d 0` underflow or silently dropping a trailing odd row.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "98b8b66ca3180d59347203b800094f87002d57be",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
